{# terminology: a glossary callout (green trim, open-book icon) for spelling out what a term
   means; distinct from `commentary` (a grey aside).  Mirrors the commentary signature:
   (content, title). #}
{% macro terminology(content="", title='Terminology')-%}{{admonition("terminology", title, content)}}{%- endmacro -%}

{# protocol: a tight, focused callout describing ONE cmk protocol.  `name` is the carrier (a
   `__dunder__` registry, or an interface name); `summary` is a one-line role; `surface` (optional)
   names how it is queried / conformed to.  Reused across concept pages so every protocol reads the
   same way; built on the `terminology` admonition, keep `summary` / `surface` to a single line each
   (the admonition body is not re-indented, so use `<br>` / inline markup, not paragraph breaks). #}
{# protocol(...): a callout describing ONE cmk protocol.  `name` (a `__dunder__`) rides the
   TITLE bar as `<glyph> Protocol: <name>`, with a black RHS link to the canonical Protocols
   concept when `mkdocs` is passed -- so the body carries only the summary, no name preamble.
   Pass `mkdocs` at every call site. #}
{# protocol: a STRUCTURED card for one `cmk.protocol`, shaped like the algebra cards -- fixed
   labeled fields (Capability / Requires / Tier / Surface / Notes).  Each field renders as a
   bold label paragraph followed by an indented body paragraph (the algebra `_section` shape;
   the `.protocol` section CSS keys on the `strong:only-child` label).  Terse, capitalized, no
   em-dashes. #}
{% macro protocol(name, capability='', requires='', tier='', surface='', notes='', mkdocs={}, open=false)-%}
<a name="{{ (name|lower|replace('_','')|replace('.','')|replace(' ','-')) }}-protocols"></a>

{{ '???+' if open else '???' }} protocol "`{{ name }}`{% if mkdocs %}<a class='protocol-doclink' href='{{ mkdocs.site_relative_url }}/cmk/concepts/#protocols'>Protocol</a>{% endif %}"
{% for row in [['Capability', capability], ['Requires', requires], ['Tier', tier], ['Surface', surface], ['Notes', notes]] if row[1] %}
    **{{ row[0] }}:**

    {{ row[1] }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{# non_core: the standardized "this is an opt-in, non-core plugin/module" banner for a
   feature's own page.  Consolidates the divergent Non-core / "Opt-in plugin" banners onto one
   title + type + boilerplate.  `name` = the file (e.g. `tux.repl.cmk`); `kind` = 'plugin' |
   'module'; `detail` = an optional trailing clause (extra requirements / behavior); `@/` in
   `detail` expands to a site-relative link.  Cross-references FROM core pages keep their own
   phrasing; this is for a feature describing itself. #}
{% macro non_core(name, kind='plugin', detail='', mkdocs={}) -%}
{%- set _d = ('  ' ~ detail.replace('@/', mkdocs.site_relative_url ~ '/')) if detail else '' -%}
{{ admonition("warning", "Optional Plugin / Module", "This is the non-core `" ~ name ~ "` " ~ kind ~ ", not part of always-loaded `compose.mk`; load it via the [plugin system](" ~ mkdocs.site_relative_url ~ "/plugins/overview)." ~ _d) }}
{%- endmacro -%}


